      "answer": "To save a checklist array to `localStorage`, you first convert the array to a JSON string using `JSON.stringify()`. Then, use `localStorage.setItem(key, value)` to store it. For example, to save a checklist named 'myList': `localStorage.setItem('myList', JSON.stringify(['item1', 'item2']))`. To restore it, retrieve the string using `localStorage.getItem('myList')` and parse it back into an array using `JSON.parse()`. Finally, you can use `JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('myList'))` to get the original array. Sources: MDN Web Docs for `localStorage` and `Storage.setItem()`.\n\nSources read:\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/localStorage\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Storage/setItem"
